  "id": "DrugBank_DB00959 - MONDO_grouped_5306_20655",
  "verbalization": "Methylprednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ankylosing Spondylitis through a multi-step pathway involving inflammatory mediators. The evidence suggests that Methylprednisolone is linked to Psoriatic Arthritis, which in turn is associated with Infliximab and then with Ankylosing Spondylitis. This indicates a potential role of Methylprednisolone in modulating inflammatory responses that contribute to the development of Ankylosing Spondylitis. The presence of overlapping indications with Infliximab, a TNF inhibitor, suggests that Methylprednisolone may act as a complementary agent in the treatment of inflammatory conditions, possibly by reducing inflammation or enhancing the effects of other therapies. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex interplay between steroid hormones and inflammatory mediators in the progression of Ankylosing Spondylitis, emphasizing the importance of considering both direct and indirect mechanisms in drug repurposing efforts.",
